  "notes": [
    "The native reader renders the publisher's immutable Hafs and Warsh JSON verse corpora; the verified PDFs remain bundled only as independent canonical audit references.",
    "The source JSON is never rewritten. When the matching publisher font is unavailable, the rendering derivative removes only the terminal KFG presentation-form ayah marker and draws the edition-local aya_no as a separate medallion; search and storage retain the exact source string.",
    "Muyassar Ghareeb v0.1 contains Arabic word meanings for the Hafs reference and is not a full tafsir.",
    "Full Tafsir Muyassar v3 is intentionally excluded because the obtained file did not match the publisher's published integrity checksum.",
    "QuranEnc translations are verbatim, versioned SQLite snapshots for the Hafs verse-numbering reference only; they are translations of meanings and never replace the KFGQPC Arabic text.",
    "Warsh translations remain excluded because its 6,214 edition-local verse boundaries cannot be joined safely to the 6,236-row Hafs translation key space.",
    "Reader typography: the KFGQPC publisher fonts render the corpora exactly as printed (embedded ayah-mark symbols); Amiri Quran and Harmattan are optional reviewed faces for which the renderer strips publisher marker symbols and draws standard U+06DD ayah signs instead. Qur'an letters and diacritics are never altered."
  ],
